.TH MORTY "1" "2026" "morty" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
morty \- Privacy aware web content sanitizer proxy as a service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B morty
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Morty rewrites web pages to exclude malicious HTML tags and attributes. It
also replaces external resource references to prevent third party
information leaks.
.sp
The main goal of morty is to provide a result proxy for searx and
compatible SearXNG setups, but it can be used as a standalone sanitizer
service too.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB\-allow\fR string
.IP
Comma separated host suffix allowlist. When set, only matching hosts are
proxified.
.HP
\fB\-allowprivate\fR
.IP
Allow requests to private/reserved IP ranges (loopback, link-local, RFC1918,
CGNAT, multicast, documentation ranges). Disabled by default to prevent SSRF
abuse.
.HP
\fB\-cache\fR uint
.IP
Response cache size in MB for static content. 0 disables the cache (default).
.HP
\fB\-cachettl\fR uint
.IP
Response cache entry TTL in seconds (default 300).
.HP
\fB\-debug\fR
.IP
Debug mode: verbose request and error logging (default true).
.HP
\fB\-deny\fR string
.IP
Comma separated host suffix denylist. Deny matches always win.
.HP
\fB\-followredirect\fR
.IP
Follow HTTP GET redirects.
.HP
\fB\-ipv6\fR
.IP
Allow IPv6 HTTP requests (default true).
.HP
\fB\-key\fR string
.IP
HMAC url validation key (base64 encoded) \- leave blank to disable
validation.
.HP
\fB\-keyttl\fR uint
.IP
Signed url lifetime in seconds. 0 disables expiry (default). When set, every
signed link carries a mortyexp timestamp folded into the HMAC and
non-expiring links are rejected.
.HP
\fB\-listen\fR string
.IP
Listen address (default "127.0.0.1:3000").
.HP
\fB\-metrics\fR
.IP
Enable the /metrics endpoint (Prometheus text format).
.HP
\fB\-proxy\fR string
.IP
Use the specified HTTP proxy (ie: '[user:pass@]hostname:port'). Overrides
\-socks5, \-ipv6.
.HP
\fB\-proxyenv\fR
.IP
Use a HTTP proxy as set in the environment (HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY and
NO_PROXY). Overrides \-proxy, \-socks5, \-ipv6.
.HP
\fB\-ratelimit\fR uint
.IP
Requests per minute per client IP when no key is set (default 60). 0
disables.
.HP
\fB\-socks5\fR string
.IP
Use a SOCKS5 proxy (ie: 'hostname:port'). Overrides \-ipv6.
.HP
\fB\-timeout\fR uint
.IP
Request timeout in seconds, 1 to 3600 (default 5).
.HP
\fB\-ua\fR string
.IP
Upstream User-Agent header.
.HP
\fB\-version\fR
.IP
Show version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Morty can be configured with the following environment variables, matching
the flags above: MORTY_ADDRESS, MORTY_KEY, MORTY_KEYTTL, DEBUG, MORTY_DEBUG,
MORTY_IPV6, MORTY_TIMEOUT, MORTY_FOLLOWREDIRECT, MORTY_ALLOWPRIVATE,
MORTY_RATELIMIT, MORTY_UA, MORTY_ALLOW, MORTY_DENY, MORTY_METRICS,
MORTY_CACHE, MORTY_CACHETTL.
.SH BUGS
Bugs or suggestions? Visit the issue tracker at
https://github.com/Sudo-Ivan/morty-xng/issues.
